    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, this is a good start and definitely more organized. But I just checked the preview in the auditor's tool and the thoroughness score is still coming back a bit low. It's looking for a much deeper level of structural complexity. \n\nCould you expand this? You don't need to add much new content—the core info is fine—but try to break everything down into even smaller, more granular subsections. Use a lot more headings to separate every single distinct requirement or detail so the tool really picks up on the \"granularity.\" Basically, the more divisions you create, the better we look to the system. Just don't make it too messy, it still needs to look professional.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
